abstract:
We investigate the topological signatures of neutral-current Non-Standard Interactions (NSI) in long-baseline neutrino oscillations by extending the open-path Pancharatnam geometric phase framework. Incorporating off-diagonal vector couplings ($\varepsilon_{e	au} = |\varepsilon_{e	au}|e^{i\phi_{e	au}}$) into the discrete-layer matter Hamiltonian across the DUNE baseline ($L = 1300	ext{ km}$), we analyze the state evolution for both neutrino ($
